WEBVTT

00:02.230 --> 00:04.920
Can you guys solve this formula?!

00:04.920 --> 00:05.220
You'll never make it into
Harvard if you can't!

00:05.220 --> 00:07.410
That's not the right equation.
You'll never make it into
Harvard if you can't!

00:07.410 --> 00:07.980
You'll never make it into
Harvard if you can't!

00:07.980 --> 00:11.740
I think it was copied from a model problem,
but they left out a line.

00:12.110 --> 00:14.740
I'm impressed you even noticed.

00:15.170 --> 00:19.560
I bet you gave your teachers a
hard time in school, didn't you?

00:19.560 --> 00:22.250
Aw, come on. I did not.

00:26.370 --> 00:28.500
Wait, now that I think about it...

00:29.310 --> 00:30.500
Maybe I did?

00:30.900 --> 00:32.010
I knew it.

02:05.730 --> 02:09.650
Looks like my class's average in the
mock exams has dropped again...

02:09.650 --> 02:10.980
Actually, no.

02:11.650 --> 02:15.480
These are typical grades for this school.

02:16.250 --> 02:20.020
But the student who was single-handedly
raising the curve a lot has gone...

02:20.020 --> 02:21.620
Yanagi-sensei?

02:21.620 --> 02:24.980
About the report for the PTA
that I asked you to do...

02:24.980 --> 02:26.040
Oh, uh...

02:26.040 --> 02:28.620
Sorry! I'll have it finished today!

02:29.390 --> 02:32.380
Being a teacher means having no breaks.

02:33.230 --> 02:35.720
Your daily classes, your lesson plans,

02:35.720 --> 02:38.600
overseeing club activities,
excursions, the PTA...

02:38.600 --> 02:42.960
And if a student causes a problem,
you need to be available 24/7 to respond.

02:42.960 --> 02:45.760
It's not even a high-paying job, either.

02:46.060 --> 02:48.770
But I'm still working hard today for my—

02:48.770 --> 02:50.200
Yanagi-sensei?
But I'm still working hard today for my—

02:51.000 --> 02:53.900
Would you like to go to an
amusement park with me?

02:54.580 --> 02:55.480
Huh?

02:55.480 --> 02:59.150
I mean, I just happened
to get two tickets, so...

02:59.430 --> 03:00.320
If you don't mind, I'd—

03:00.320 --> 03:01.230
What are you talking about, Taniguchi-sensei?
If you don't mind, I'd—

03:01.230 --> 03:03.160
What are you talking about, Taniguchi-sensei?

03:03.450 --> 03:05.500
I don't have the time!

03:05.500 --> 03:08.160
B-But don't you think it's important
to relax now and then?

03:08.160 --> 03:11.770
Don't be ridiculous. Of course not.

03:14.590 --> 03:19.670
Unbelievable. How can he think about that
sort of thing when he's a teacher, too?

03:23.040 --> 03:25.090
Huh? Yanagi-sensei?

03:25.930 --> 03:27.810
It <i>is</i> you!

03:28.310 --> 03:30.150
Oh! Yuzaki-kun!

03:30.150 --> 03:32.310
Yep! It's been a while.

03:33.160 --> 03:35.690
It really has! Have you been doing well?

03:35.690 --> 03:37.500
Yes, thank you for asking.

03:37.500 --> 03:39.940
I heard you had a pretty rough time.

03:40.330 --> 03:43.220
You were hospitalized and ended
up not going to high school.

03:43.220 --> 03:45.750
Well, it's definitely been a busy time...

03:45.750 --> 03:47.080
Busy?

03:50.080 --> 03:53.760
Yuzaki-kun, there's, uh, something
on your left ring finger.

03:53.760 --> 03:55.330
Oh, the ring?

03:55.330 --> 03:58.590
Yeah, I actually got married.

03:59.150 --> 04:03.200
Married... Married... Married... Married...

04:03.200 --> 04:05.200
D-Don't tell me, Yuzaki-kun...

04:05.200 --> 04:09.350
You became a delinquent after being unable
to enroll and got snared by a bad girl?!

04:09.590 --> 04:10.760
And let me tell you—

04:10.760 --> 04:11.980
Yuzaki-kun!

04:12.240 --> 04:14.350
It's time for a house call!

04:14.350 --> 04:15.710
Huh? But I already gradu—

04:15.710 --> 04:17.150
It's a background check!

04:17.150 --> 04:19.110
Take me to your house right now!

04:21.120 --> 04:24.060
Who might she be, darling?

04:24.060 --> 04:26.120
Er, well...

04:26.480 --> 04:28.190
I think I mentioned her before...

04:28.190 --> 04:32.120
So this is Yuzaki-kun's wife?

04:33.370 --> 04:36.840
Man, what the heck? She's really cute!

04:36.840 --> 04:37.250
Huh?

04:37.250 --> 04:39.760
You married someone this gorgeous?

04:39.760 --> 04:41.510
Y-Yeah...

04:42.980 --> 04:45.920
This is my homeroom teacher
from middle school.

04:45.920 --> 04:47.760
My name is Yanagi Naoko.

04:47.760 --> 04:49.510
Oh, you're a teacher.

04:52.470 --> 04:55.030
I apologize for not saying
this earlier, Yanagi-sensei.

04:55.030 --> 04:57.770
I'm Nasa's wife, Yuzaki Tsukasa.

04:57.770 --> 05:01.500
Oh, right! It's a pleasure to meet you.

05:03.100 --> 05:06.710
Her introducing herself as my
wife has got me flustered.

05:06.710 --> 05:10.210
She seems really nice!
Nothing like I imagined.

05:10.210 --> 05:12.290
Wait, what did you imagine?!

05:13.160 --> 05:15.590
Hang on, I can't let my guard down yet.

05:15.590 --> 05:20.160
She might have some kind of horrible secret.

05:23.040 --> 05:26.050
Would you like to join us for dinner?

05:26.050 --> 05:27.940
N-No, I couldn't!

05:27.940 --> 05:31.180
Barging into a former student's house,
and then being treated—

05:31.440 --> 05:33.430
Delicious!

05:33.430 --> 05:38.060
What is this? Do you eat delicious
meals like this every day, Yuzaki-kun?

05:38.060 --> 05:39.690
Well, yes.

05:40.240 --> 05:41.990
Please, help yourself.

05:41.990 --> 05:42.940
Really?!

05:44.590 --> 05:47.440
I can't remember the last
time I had a meal this good!

05:47.950 --> 05:52.950
It's been nothing but convenience store
food and instant noodles lately...

05:53.300 --> 05:56.960
H-Hang on, Naoko! Don't let
her suck you in so easily!

05:57.220 --> 05:58.710
Even if she's a great chef,

05:59.030 --> 06:03.180
for someone to get married so young...
There has to be some issue!

06:03.180 --> 06:05.960
This burdock root is fantastic!

06:05.960 --> 06:09.120
Right? I thought you might like it.

06:09.120 --> 06:12.970
Yeah! Everything you make
is so good, Tsukasa-chan!

06:13.320 --> 06:15.170
Isn't it, though?

06:15.170 --> 06:16.420
Look at you, master chef!

06:22.160 --> 06:23.730
I get it now...

06:24.560 --> 06:27.650
You can taste the depths of her love.

06:31.560 --> 06:33.740
Yuzaki-kun, what are you
going to do in the future?

06:33.940 --> 06:34.580
Huh?

06:34.580 --> 06:35.940
I mean, think about it.

06:35.940 --> 06:38.420
Most married people get a corporate job,

06:38.420 --> 06:40.700
or get a high school
certification and go to college.

06:41.630 --> 06:45.500
I'm honestly not thinking
about it too much right now.

06:46.770 --> 06:49.380
It's true that I could
probably get into college,

06:49.840 --> 06:52.080
and if I take on more work,
I'd probably make more money...

06:52.780 --> 06:57.520
But right now my priority is spending as
much time as possible with Tsukasa-chan.

06:57.520 --> 07:01.640
Don't you get anxious
thinking about your future?

07:01.640 --> 07:03.520
Well, you can never predict the future.

07:03.900 --> 07:08.000
Which is why I think it's
important to enjoy the present.

07:08.000 --> 07:11.780
I'm sure my future self
will figure something out.

07:13.530 --> 07:14.990
Tsukasa-chan, let me help you.

07:14.990 --> 07:16.720
Thank you, darling.

07:18.150 --> 07:20.800
Enjoy the present...

07:21.640 --> 07:23.290
Thank you for the meal.

07:23.620 --> 07:25.600
I'll see you around, Yuzaki-kun.

07:25.600 --> 07:28.620
Sure. Thanks for coming by today.

07:28.620 --> 07:30.480
Have a safe walk home, Sensei.

07:30.480 --> 07:32.300
Right. Thanks again!

07:38.000 --> 07:39.410
I see...

07:39.840 --> 07:43.700
Life is supposed to be about being happy.

07:45.040 --> 07:49.330
Every day spent just running
around being anxious

07:49.760 --> 07:53.200
is another day of that life gone forever.

08:03.130 --> 08:06.460
Hello? This is Yanagi. I was wondering...

08:07.110 --> 08:10.200
Did you still want to go
to that amusement park?

08:11.280 --> 08:12.470
Thank goodness.

08:13.120 --> 08:14.970
Then let's go together.

08:16.000 --> 08:18.650
Work? It'll be okay.

08:18.650 --> 08:21.900
My future self will figure something out.

08:23.710 --> 08:28.230
You're really looking the part of
a bathhouse clerk lately, Tsukassan.

08:28.230 --> 08:31.990
You think so? As long as
I'm being helpful, I'm glad.

08:33.390 --> 08:34.920
Welcome to...

08:34.920 --> 08:36.370
the... bathhouse?

08:38.090 --> 08:40.570
Okay, he looks scary.

08:40.570 --> 08:42.350
Y-Yeah, I guess.

08:45.060 --> 08:48.130
There a Yuzaki who lives here?

08:49.460 --> 08:50.920
That'd be me.

08:51.370 --> 08:52.920
What do you want?

08:53.470 --> 08:58.050
I'm looking for a dude called
Yuzaki Nasa, not <i>you</i>.

08:58.620 --> 09:00.040
He's here, right?

09:00.040 --> 09:03.560
Real smart guy. You write his name like
"starry sky," but say it like "Nasa."

09:04.020 --> 09:06.430
What does the yakuza want with Senpai?!

09:06.430 --> 09:07.520
Too bad.

09:09.330 --> 09:10.070
Wha?!

09:10.070 --> 09:14.000
I've got nothing to tell some
punk kid who's got no manners.

09:14.000 --> 09:17.070
This is a bathhouse. If you're
not going in, then leave.

09:17.380 --> 09:18.570
Say what?!

09:18.570 --> 09:21.080
Wh-Wh-Whoa there, Tsukassan!

09:21.080 --> 09:25.210
Aren't you scared? He might be
one of those ya-<i>youknowwhats</i>!

09:25.210 --> 09:26.830
What if he is?

09:27.860 --> 09:31.370
I have no reason to fear this twerp.

09:31.370 --> 09:35.340
Tsukassan's one of those people who
never backs down from stuff like this!

09:35.340 --> 09:38.840
So what's it gonna be? Either take a
bath or get out. Make up your mind.

09:38.840 --> 09:41.100
Y-You little...

09:41.100 --> 09:43.220
How much does it cost, then, punk?!

09:43.220 --> 09:44.830
It's 500 yen to enter!

09:44.830 --> 09:46.560
Another 1,000 if you wanna use the sauna!

09:46.560 --> 09:48.060
You can get a towel set for 1,300!

09:48.060 --> 09:50.230
And students get a
100-yen discount, you punk!

09:50.230 --> 09:52.730
Gimme the towel set, then.
For one high school student, please!

09:52.730 --> 09:56.240
Thank you very much! You can get your
ticket at the machine over there!

09:58.610 --> 10:00.740
Who the hell are you supposed to be?

10:01.090 --> 10:03.280
I should be asking you that.

10:03.280 --> 10:07.500
If you mean any harm to my husband,
you're gonna suffer for it.

10:08.320 --> 10:09.000
Oh!

10:09.330 --> 10:11.800
It's Ginga-kun! Good to see you again.

10:13.450 --> 10:15.140
Big Bro Nasa!

10:15.140 --> 10:16.700
It's been a while, sir.

10:17.520 --> 10:19.580
G-Ginga-kun?

10:21.550 --> 10:25.000
Senpai, is this guy a relative of yours?

10:25.000 --> 10:27.510
Yep. This is Ginga-kun, my cousin.

10:27.510 --> 10:29.520
How'd you guess?

10:30.420 --> 10:32.900
The name helped, I'd say.

10:33.600 --> 10:36.160
He's your cousin, darling?

10:36.160 --> 10:38.800
Yep! Onimaru Ginga-kun.

10:38.800 --> 10:40.570
He's 17 years old and in high school.

10:40.570 --> 10:44.790
Bro, I gotta ask, who's this lady?

10:44.790 --> 10:47.610
Oh, I didn't introduce you yet!

10:47.610 --> 10:49.640
See, I got married.

10:49.640 --> 10:51.540
This is my wife, Tsukasa-chan.

10:51.540 --> 10:53.790
Y-Your wife?!

10:54.130 --> 10:54.760
Yep.

10:55.200 --> 10:59.420
Bro... When did you climb the
stairway to adulthood?

10:59.870 --> 11:01.330
Whoa! Ginga-kun?!

11:01.330 --> 11:03.430
Ginga-kun!

11:04.310 --> 11:06.650
I'm so sorry!

11:06.650 --> 11:10.960
I had no idea my bro was
married, and I acted real rude!

11:10.960 --> 11:13.980
I'm sorry, too. I really
should've told you already.

11:14.460 --> 11:17.840
Darling, he's not in the yakuza, is he?

11:17.840 --> 11:21.490
Aw, come on! Ginga-kun's a
normal high school student.

11:22.160 --> 11:27.280
He does a lot of extracurricular activities.
He's even the student council president.

11:27.280 --> 11:30.500
Yes, sir. I'm running my own crew.

11:30.910 --> 11:33.380
You're <i>sure</i> he's a high school student?

11:33.790 --> 11:38.000
Big Bro Nasa here's had my
back since I was a runt.

11:38.000 --> 11:42.010
I've basically been chasing
him my whole life.

11:42.300 --> 11:44.410
The other day, we had a
beef with another squad,

11:44.410 --> 11:47.560
and he gave me some advice
on how to squash it.

11:48.040 --> 11:50.420
Oh, when I helped you win your athletic meet

11:50.420 --> 11:52.860
by teaching you about
Clausewitz's theory of war?

11:52.860 --> 11:55.060
So when he says "another squad,"
he means a different school?

11:55.360 --> 11:59.440
He gave me some advice on
how to survive a raid, too.

11:59.790 --> 12:03.120
Right, that was how to handle pop quizzes.

12:03.120 --> 12:05.660
So, "surviving" in academic terms?

12:05.990 --> 12:10.270
Bro's advice has got our earnings up, too,

12:10.270 --> 12:12.360
which has made the boss happy.

12:12.360 --> 12:13.640
The... boss?

12:13.640 --> 12:15.790
Maybe he means the principal?

12:16.070 --> 12:18.850
But before I get down to it...

12:18.850 --> 12:22.140
I gotta ask you something, Bro.

12:22.790 --> 12:23.590
What's that?

12:24.220 --> 12:27.930
I know it ain't exactly cool to ask, but...

12:28.350 --> 12:31.310
Wh-Why'd you get married?

12:32.360 --> 12:35.310
Why? Well,

12:36.050 --> 12:37.640
because I love her, I'd say.

12:37.640 --> 12:40.820
Seriously, don't say that stuff
in front of other people!

12:41.480 --> 12:42.440
In that case...

12:42.800 --> 12:45.280
C-Can you, like, kiss her?

12:47.780 --> 12:50.610
How am I supposed to buy that
it's true love otherwise?!

12:50.610 --> 12:54.290
If it's for real, you could kiss
her in front of me, right?!

12:54.290 --> 12:56.850
What the heck are you talking about, man?!

12:56.850 --> 12:58.920
It's a big deal!

12:59.390 --> 13:02.350
If you're his wife,
you're practically a sister to me!

13:02.350 --> 13:05.440
That means I'm ready to put
my life on the line for you!

13:05.440 --> 13:08.300
And I ain't gonna do that
unless this is the real deal!

13:08.300 --> 13:09.920
Gin-san's right!

13:09.920 --> 13:14.280
How am I supposed to believe your love's for
real when I never hear any moaning at night?!

13:14.280 --> 13:15.810
So you may kiss the bride!

13:15.810 --> 13:17.640
Are you two stupid or something?!

13:17.640 --> 13:20.380
Darling, say something!

13:20.380 --> 13:21.160
I don't mind.

13:22.510 --> 13:26.150
I have absolutely no doubts about
my love for you, Tsukasa-chan.

13:26.150 --> 13:28.760
So I don't mind letting them see us kiss.

13:28.760 --> 13:31.100
Well, maybe you should?!

13:31.100 --> 13:33.700
But if you're too embarrassed...

13:34.320 --> 13:36.710
Then I want to respect that.

13:42.430 --> 13:46.220
F-Fine... then.

13:52.220 --> 13:54.220
I-I get it already!

13:55.760 --> 13:58.840
I can tell you two really love each other.

13:59.320 --> 14:01.150
So that's enough.

14:01.410 --> 14:03.350
Huh? Really?

14:03.350 --> 14:05.740
Yeah. It's plenty.

14:06.380 --> 14:11.120
Besides, I don't really wanna
see something so... scandalous.

14:12.240 --> 14:14.140
It was your idea in the first place!

14:14.140 --> 14:18.210
Why'd you stop it at the good part?!
You weenie yakuza!

14:18.210 --> 14:21.640
Sis, please! Calm down! I'm begging you!

14:23.160 --> 14:26.990
So what actually brought
you by today, Ginga-kun?

14:26.990 --> 14:30.760
I actually need your
brains for something, Bro.

14:31.150 --> 14:34.160
This had better not involve bank fraud.

14:34.160 --> 14:35.390
Come on.

14:35.700 --> 14:38.560
First, I've got something you need to see.

14:38.560 --> 14:39.420
Hey!

14:40.190 --> 14:43.120
All right, boys! Handle it carefully,
or you're dead!

14:43.120 --> 14:43.650
Yes, sir!

14:46.200 --> 14:47.630
Pardon us!

14:48.460 --> 14:52.410
This is what I need your
help with, Big Bro Nasa.

14:55.410 --> 14:57.310
Isn't that...

14:57.310 --> 15:00.280
It's one of those things used
for carrying another thing.

15:02.300 --> 15:05.480
It really is a cat! You took in a cat?!

15:05.480 --> 15:11.210
Yeah. One of my boys found him collapsed
this morning. Seems to have lost his mom.

15:11.210 --> 15:13.300
Wait, why'd you bring him here?!

15:13.600 --> 15:17.810
Well, it's kinda our fault, but...

15:18.700 --> 15:22.230
At first we figured we could just
feed it, then drop it back off,

15:22.570 --> 15:25.630
but it seems like if you abandon
a cat after taking it in,

15:25.630 --> 15:28.360
you're in violation of animal welfare laws.

15:29.740 --> 15:32.740
It ain't like we can turn to the cops,

15:33.070 --> 15:35.870
so we been looking for an owner,
trying to find out if he's lost.

15:36.480 --> 15:40.540
The whole crew's been freaking
out since we picked him up.

15:40.860 --> 15:42.620
Well, you're a real
precious bunch, aren't you?!

15:42.960 --> 15:47.200
Which is why I figured
I should turn to you, Bro.

15:47.200 --> 15:51.600
I remembered you took real good
care of a cat back in the day.

15:52.430 --> 15:53.480
Is that right?

15:53.480 --> 15:54.170
Yeah.

15:54.820 --> 15:56.510
But I have to say, Ginga-kun...

15:57.560 --> 16:00.780
You took that kitten in, and then came here?

16:01.640 --> 16:03.650
The first stop you should've
made was the vet.

16:04.170 --> 16:04.880
Yes, sir!

16:04.880 --> 16:07.600
All right, people, bring the car around!

16:07.600 --> 16:08.650
Yes, sir!

16:11.280 --> 16:14.160
Oh, you took in a kitten?

16:14.160 --> 16:16.720
Yes. We'd like to check
for viruses and parasites,

16:16.720 --> 16:22.160
get flea and tick treatment,
and have him groomed after the checkup.

16:22.480 --> 16:26.170
And if they're available,
the FVRCP immunizations!

16:26.170 --> 16:28.650
Oh, sure thing. You know your stuff.

16:28.650 --> 16:31.630
We'll be holding on to him
for about two hours, then.

16:31.630 --> 16:34.160
So, what's his name?

16:34.160 --> 16:37.320
Uh, I wouldn't really know...

16:37.730 --> 16:39.930
We haven't even seen him yet.

16:39.930 --> 16:42.430
I'll let him out for a bit, then.

16:50.240 --> 16:52.440
That is weirdly menacing.

16:53.830 --> 16:56.120
Well, he's certainly lively!

16:56.120 --> 16:57.950
Uh, he's really gnawing on you there!

16:58.270 --> 17:02.400
It's quite all right.
So, what should I call him?

17:02.400 --> 17:04.510
Wh-What do you think?

17:04.510 --> 17:05.980
Let's see...

17:08.110 --> 17:11.480
His back is brown
with a white square on it...

17:11.910 --> 17:13.090
Let's go with Toast.

17:13.360 --> 17:15.520
Huh? T-Toast?

17:15.520 --> 17:17.580
Yeah! It's cute, right?

17:21.600 --> 17:25.350
Well, at least his name
should be cute, I guess.

17:26.240 --> 17:28.240
So what are we going to do with him?

17:28.240 --> 17:31.250
Well, even if we look for
someone to adopt him,

17:31.250 --> 17:34.110
we'll have to look after him
for the time being, at least.

17:34.520 --> 17:37.690
I'd feel uneasy about letting
Ginga-kun and his friends handle it...

17:37.690 --> 17:42.040
And a proper checkup means holding on
to him for at least two or three months.

17:42.040 --> 17:46.700
If we can't find anyone to
adopt Toast, should we do it?

17:52.540 --> 17:56.130
To be honest, I'm not feeling
too confident about that.

17:56.130 --> 17:57.840
I hear you.

17:57.840 --> 18:00.850
Bro! How's the kid doing?!

18:01.590 --> 18:03.720
Oh, he seems good.

18:03.720 --> 18:07.520
That's a big relief. Hate to
see a sick kid, y'know?

18:08.020 --> 18:12.560
We'll look after him for the time being,
so we're about to go shopping.

18:12.560 --> 18:15.000
For real?! That's a huge relief!

18:15.000 --> 18:17.020
In that case, we can grab the stuff for you.

18:17.020 --> 18:22.120
My boys can get all the white powder
and pieces you might need.

18:22.120 --> 18:24.150
Let's word things differently, okay?

18:24.150 --> 18:26.910
Lemme just have them go and grab it.

18:27.420 --> 18:29.660
It's not that simple, Ginga-kun.

18:30.420 --> 18:33.210
You need to make sure the kitty
litter is safe to ingest.

18:33.210 --> 18:36.530
And watch out for stuff
with a synthetic base.

18:36.530 --> 18:39.660
Even the natural stuff can have
antimicrobials, deodorizers,

18:39.660 --> 18:42.300
and other synthetic stuff
mixed in, which is a no-go.

18:42.300 --> 18:46.690
For food, make sure it's a kind
that's safe for people to eat.

18:46.690 --> 18:49.440
Nothing labeled "oatmeal" that's
made out of mystery ingredients.

18:49.440 --> 18:53.280
And a lot of the cheaper stuff uses
grains that are hard for cats to digest,

18:53.280 --> 18:53.780
so let's avoid those and—

18:53.780 --> 18:55.070
Slow down a sec!
so let's avoid those and—

18:55.360 --> 18:57.880
Anyway, making sure a pet stays healthy

18:57.880 --> 19:01.950
requires a fair amount of knowledge, effort,
and resources. Good luck with the search.

19:03.140 --> 19:04.350
Got it!

19:05.280 --> 19:08.310
You know a lot about cats, darling.

19:08.310 --> 19:11.550
Well, people can manage their own health,

19:11.950 --> 19:13.960
but pets don't have that option.

19:14.800 --> 19:19.220
Their health is their owner's responsibility,
and it's a serious one.

19:19.670 --> 19:23.470
Any pet you take care
of is bound to be happy.

19:23.470 --> 19:25.470
Y-You think so?

19:25.470 --> 19:27.660
Sorry about the wait.

19:27.660 --> 19:30.400
There didn't seem to be any problems.

19:31.230 --> 19:34.260
That's a relief. Was he a handful?

19:34.260 --> 19:37.920
Nope, he settled down a lot
after having some food.

19:37.920 --> 19:39.490
Good for you, Toast.

19:40.130 --> 19:41.970
Seems like you're healthy!

19:42.670 --> 19:44.240
Aw, stop that.

19:44.980 --> 19:50.000
I realized that when you add cute
to cute, the result is double cute.

19:50.400 --> 19:51.970
Okay, let's head home.

19:51.970 --> 19:54.640
You're part of the family now, Toast.

19:56.560 --> 19:58.590
Why?!

20:13.020 --> 20:14.530
What's wrong?

20:18.380 --> 20:21.610
Is he asking to be fed?

20:22.500 --> 20:24.360
Ugh, it's still the middle of the night.

20:24.970 --> 20:26.120
Is it just me...

20:27.150 --> 20:30.680
or have I been marked as the
one it's okay to wake up?

20:36.880 --> 20:40.000
Wow, he's really scarfing it down.

20:43.480 --> 20:47.010
Oh, and now that he's got a full stomach,
he's lost interest in me.

20:54.800 --> 20:57.900
Huh? Is it me, or is this a huge
difference in treatment?

20:59.490 --> 21:01.900
That must've been rough, waking
up in the middle of the night.

21:01.900 --> 21:05.830
But I think that means
he trusts you, darling.

21:05.830 --> 21:07.140
Is that it?

21:07.140 --> 21:07.910
Of course.

21:08.290 --> 21:09.510
He's just like me in that sense,

21:09.510 --> 21:12.910
which is why he'll turn to you
for attention from time to time.

21:14.810 --> 21:17.780
Tsukasa-chan, you want attention from me?

21:17.780 --> 21:18.870
Of course.

21:21.180 --> 21:25.930
You think I'd sleep so defenselessly
around someone I didn't trust?

21:29.300 --> 21:30.680
But I have to say...

21:31.130 --> 21:33.200
Cats are really cute.

21:33.200 --> 21:35.400
Y-Yeah...

21:36.250 --> 21:39.310
But you are, too, Tsukasa-chan.

21:42.770 --> 21:46.990
Then... between me and Toast, who's cuter?

21:46.990 --> 21:49.450
Well, uh...

21:50.630 --> 21:51.940
Well what?

21:58.890 --> 22:01.060
How long have you been there, Kaname-chan?!

22:01.060 --> 22:03.970
Since around the time you were
getting into the newlywed routine.

22:03.970 --> 22:05.970
I-It's not what you think it is!

22:10.030 --> 22:13.790
Tsukasa-chan, look! Toast is eating.

22:14.420 --> 22:17.650
Hey, you're right. He's so cute.

22:19.010 --> 22:21.100
H-He really is...

22:21.590 --> 22:22.480
That's right.

22:23.140 --> 22:25.480
Since she just got out of the bath,

22:25.480 --> 22:28.490
she smells really amazing up close.

22:31.620 --> 22:32.890
Darling?

22:34.000 --> 22:36.130
Oh, is that why you called me over?

22:36.130 --> 22:38.610
N-No, I mean...

22:38.610 --> 22:42.460
You said you wanted attention
from me this afternoon, so...

22:43.530 --> 22:44.820
I was wondering how...

22:45.600 --> 22:48.760
exactly... you wanted attention, so...

22:49.360 --> 22:51.010
I will admit it...

22:51.290 --> 22:54.490
I've been wanting more attention lately.

23:07.070 --> 23:09.450
U-Uh, Toast?

23:09.450 --> 23:12.030
C-Could you turn away for a sec?

23:14.410 --> 23:15.480
Wait, no...

23:15.480 --> 23:17.910
I'll give you a treat later, okay?

23:18.580 --> 23:20.440
C-Come on, seriously...

23:20.440 --> 23:23.650
Just five seconds. We'll be
done in five seconds, okay?

23:25.650 --> 23:29.090
Next up is "That Time I Reincarnated
in a Dreamy Magical Kingdom."

23:29.090 --> 23:31.770
I hear you can go these days
without needing to reincarnate first.

23:31.770 --> 23:33.050
And it's right near the city.

23:33.050 --> 23:35.050
You know what that means! Let's go!

23:35.050 --> 23:39.930
Just you wait! I'll see right through
their stupid lovey-dovey magic!
